/*
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Resources for a large Kraken2 database in the stock purity check
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Kraken2 loads hash.k2d into memory in full, so this step needs at least that file's
    size. The default label gives it 8 GB, which suits the viral database and nothing
    larger. KRAKEN2_CLASSIFY refuses to start when it was given less than the database
    needs, and names the file to change.

        nextflow run . -entry BUILD_STOCK_REFERENCE ... -c conf/kraken2_large_db.example.config

    Index sizes, from the Kraken2 index collection:

        Viral           0.6 GB      the default is enough
        Standard-8      7.5 GB      8 GB is marginal, give it 10
        Standard-16    14.9 GB      the setting below
        PlusPF-16      14.9 GB      the setting below
        PlusPF, full  103.4 GB      a cluster node, see the README
        core_nt       238.2 GB      a cluster node with a lot of memory

    Scale the number to the database you downloaded. These are not defaults.
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
*/

process {
    withName: KRAKEN2_CLASSIFY {
        cpus   = 8
        memory = 18.GB
        time   = 4.h
    }
}
